{"id":"h6-01-p1","title":"Design a URL shortener (and Pastebin)","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: requirements, API, estimates, ID generation, redirect path, caching, analytics, Pastebin variant. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"requirements","title":"Requirements","html":"<p><strong>A URL shortener turns a long link into a tiny one (<code>sho.rt/aZ3k9Q</code>) and, when someone opens the tiny link, sends them to the long one.</strong> That is the whole product. Bitly, TinyURL and Twitter's t.co do this. Pastebin is the same shape with text instead of a URL.</p>\n<p><strong>Functional requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Create a short link from a long URL (optionally a custom alias and an expiry).</li>\n<li>Open a short link and get redirected to the long URL.</li>\n<li>Optional: click analytics, delete or expire a link, per-user dashboard.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Non-functional requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Redirect latency under 50 ms p99 (it sits in the path of every click).</li>\n<li>Availability 99.99% for redirects; creation can tolerate a bit less.</li>\n<li>Links must not collide and should not be easily guessable or enumerable.</li>\n<li>Read-heavy: about 100 reads for every 1 write.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 461.2 130\" width=\"461.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The two flows of the system\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M297.2 34 L353.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M297.2 34 L353.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M297.2 96 L353.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M297.2 96 L353.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M297.2 96 L353.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M297.2 96 L353.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Creator</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Visitor</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Create API</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redirect service</text><rect x=\"353.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"401.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Link store</text><rect x=\"353.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"401.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Long URL</text></svg><figcaption>The two flows of the system</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Choose 301 vs 302 now: a 301 (permanent) is cached by browsers forever, so you lose click analytics and can never change the target. A 302 (temporary) costs you a hit per click but keeps control. Bitly uses 301 for some cases and tracks clicks anyway through other means; if analytics matter, use 302. It is reversible only for new links, because browsers already cached old 301s.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A coat-check ticket: a tiny numbered tag stands for a big bulky coat stored in the back.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Starting to design before asking about analytics, expiry and custom aliases.</li>\n<li>Using 301 and then being asked how you count clicks.</li>\n<li>Not stating the read:write ratio.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"api","title":"API","html":"<p>Two public endpoints plus a few management ones. Keep them REST and idempotent where possible.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">POST /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/links</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Authorization: Bearer &#x3C;api_key></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"longUrl\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"https://example.com/a/very/long/path?x=1\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"customAlias\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"summer-sale\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,     </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// optional</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"expiresAt\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"2027-01-01T00:00:00Z\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }   </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// optional</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">201</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Created</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"shortCode\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"aZ3k9Q\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"shortUrl\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"https://sho.rt/aZ3k9Q\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"longUrl\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"https://example.com/a/very/long/path?x=1\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  \"expiresAt\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"2027-01-01T00:00:00Z\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">409</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Conflict   -> customAlias already taken</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">400</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Bad Request -> invalid or blocked URL</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">429</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Too Many Requests -> per-key limit hit</span></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">GET /aZ</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">3</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">k</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">9</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Q</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">302</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Found</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Location: https:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">//example.com/a/very/long/path?x=1</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Cache-Control: private, max-age=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">404</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Not Found -> unknown code</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">410</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Gone      -> expired or deleted</span></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">GET    /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/links/aZ</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">3</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">k</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">9</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Q/stats?from=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">2026-11-01</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">&#x26;to=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">2026-11-09</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"clicks\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">12873</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"byDay\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">...</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">], </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"topCountries\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">...</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">] }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">DELETE /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/links/aZ</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">3</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">k</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">9</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Q        -> </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">204</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Idempotency: creating the same long URL twice may return the same code (dedupe by hash) or a new one. Decide and say it. Bitly returns a new link per user; many designs dedupe per user only.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry example.</strong> Bitly's public API is exactly this: POST to create, GET on the short domain redirects, a separate stats endpoint.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A reception desk: one window to register a new tag, another window that reads a tag and points you to the room.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Putting analytics counters inside the redirect API response path synchronously.</li>\n<li>Forgetting 404 vs 410 and error codes.</li>\n<li>No auth or rate limit on the create endpoint (spam and phishing).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"estimates","title":"Estimates","html":"<p>Assume 100M new links per month, 100:1 read:write.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Quantity</th>\n<th>Calculation</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Write QPS</td>\n<td>100M / (30 x 86,400 s = 2.6M s)</td>\n<td>about 40/s, peak 120/s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Read QPS</td>\n<td>40 x 100</td>\n<td>about 4,000/s, peak 12,000/s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Record size</td>\n<td>code 7 B + long URL ~200 B + metadata ~50 B</td>\n<td>~300 B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Storage in 5 years</td>\n<td>100M x 12 x 5 = 6B links x 300 B</td>\n<td>~1.8 TB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bandwidth out</td>\n<td>4,000/s x ~500 B response</td>\n<td>~2 MB/s (tiny)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cache size (hot 20%)</td>\n<td>20% of daily reads' unique links</td>\n<td>~tens of GB, fits in one Redis</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Code length.</strong> Base62 (a-z, A-Z, 0-9). 62^6 = 56.8 billion, 62^7 = 3.5 trillion. 6B links in 5 years fits in 7 characters with a big safety margin; 6 characters would be close to the limit once collisions and waste are included. So use 7.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 432.4 68\" width=\"432.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Scale is small: one primary DB plus cache handles it\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M274.4 34 L330.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M274.4 34 L330.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">12k reads/s</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"222.79999999999998\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis cache</text><rect x=\"330.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"375.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Link DB</text></svg><figcaption>Scale is small: one primary DB plus cache handles it</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>What this tells you.</strong> 12,000 reads/s is easy for a cache; 1.8 TB is easy for one sharded or even single big Postgres/Cassandra cluster. The hard part is <strong>ID generation without collisions</strong> and <strong>cache efficiency</strong>, not raw throughput.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Counting how many coat tickets you hand out per day before deciding how big the coat room is.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Computing QPS with 86,400 s/day but monthly numbers (units mismatch).</li>\n<li>Choosing a 5-character code and not checking the keyspace.</li>\n<li>Over-sharding a 2 TB dataset on day one.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"high-level-design","title":"High-level design","html":"<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 1039.6 254\" width=\"1039.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Read path (hot) and write path\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 127 L158 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 127 L158 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 127 L331.6 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 127 L331.6 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M470.8 96 L526.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M470.8 96 L526.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M470.8 96 L526.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M470.8 96 L526.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 127 L158 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 127 L158 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 127 L331.6 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 127 L331.6 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M470.8 158 L526.8 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M470.8 158 L526.8 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M470.8 158 L526.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M470.8 158 L526.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M470.8 96 L526.8 220\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M470.8 96 L526.8 220\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M637.1999999999999 220 L693.1999999999999 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M637.1999999999999 220 L693.1999999999999 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M839.5999999999999 127 L895.5999999999999 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M839.5999999999999 127 L895.5999999999999 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"105\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"105\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Load balancer</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"74\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"401.20000000000005\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redirect service</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"136\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"401.20000000000005\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Create service</text><rect x=\"526.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"582\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis cache</text><rect x=\"526.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"582\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Link DB</text><rect x=\"526.8\" y=\"136\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"582\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ID generator</text><rect x=\"526.8\" y=\"198\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"582\" y=\"224\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Click queue</text><rect x=\"693.1999999999999\" y=\"105\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"766.4\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Analytics workers</text><rect x=\"895.5999999999999\" y=\"105\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"961.5999999999999\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Analytics store</text></svg><figcaption>Read path (hot) and write path</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Components</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Redirect service</strong>: stateless, looks up code in Redis, falls back to the DB, returns 302.</li>\n<li><strong>Create service</strong>: validates URL, gets a unique ID, base62-encodes it, stores <code>(code, longUrl, userId, createdAt, expiresAt)</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Link DB</strong>: key-value access by code. DynamoDB or Cassandra fit well (point lookups, easy sharding); Postgres also works at this size.</li>\n<li><strong>Click queue</strong>: a Kafka topic; the redirect fires and forgets an event so latency is unaffected.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Choose a key-value style store keyed by <code>shortCode</code>. Alternatives: relational with an index. It breaks if you later need rich queries (\"all links of user X sorted by date\") on the same store; solve with a secondary index or a second table. Moving store is a one-way door only in effort (data migration), not in correctness, because the access pattern is just get/put by key.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Bitly's published engineering posts describe sharded MySQL with caching; many modern clones use DynamoDB or Cassandra.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A front desk (redirect) with a fast pigeonhole shelf (cache) in front of the big archive room (DB).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Drawing an SQL join-heavy schema for what is a key-value lookup.</li>\n<li>Putting analytics writes in the redirect transaction.</li>\n<li>No cache in front of the DB for a 100:1 read workload.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"deep-dives","title":"Deep dives","html":"<h3>ID generation and collisions</h3>\n<p>How do we get a unique 7-char code? Three options:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Hash the long URL</strong> (MD5/SHA-256, take first 43 bits and base62). Simple, same URL gives same code, but collisions happen (birthday paradox: with 6B items and 3.5T keyspace, collisions are frequent). You must check the DB and retry with a salt. Extra read per write.</li>\n<li><strong>Counter + base62.</strong> A global auto-increment ID (for example from a ticket server or a range allocator) encoded in base62. No collisions by construction. Downside: codes are sequential and guessable, and a single counter is a bottleneck/SPOF.</li>\n<li><strong>Pre-generated key service (KGS).</strong> A background job fills a table of random unused 7-char keys; app servers each pull a batch of, say, 1,000 keys into memory. No collision, no coordination per request, not guessable. If a server dies you lose at most its batch (acceptable waste).</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 452.8 130\" width=\"452.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Range allocation: each app server grabs a block of IDs\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M288.8 65 L344.8 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M288.8 65 L344.8 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M122.4 96 L178.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 96 L178.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server 1</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server 2</text><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"43\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"233.60000000000002\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ID allocator</text><rect x=\"344.8\" y=\"43\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"392.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Counter DB</text></svg><figcaption>Range allocation: each app server grabs a block of IDs</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Chosen:</strong> range allocator (each server leases 10,000 IDs from a counter in ZooKeeper/DB) then scramble the number with a reversible shuffle (a Feistel permutation or multiply by a large odd prime mod 62^7) before base62, so codes are not sequential. Reversible and cheap.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># Reversible scramble so sequential ids look random</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">M </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 62</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">**</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">7</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">K </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 2654435761</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">          # odd, coprime with M</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">def</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> scramble</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(n):  </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (n </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">*</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> K) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">%</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> M</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> The ID scheme is a one-way door: once codes are public they live forever; changing the scheme later means supporting both. When it breaks: the allocator being down stops creates (reads still work), so run it replicated or let servers keep a buffer.</p>\n<h3>Redirect path and caching</h3>\n<p>Read path: LB, redirect service, Redis <code>GET code</code>. On miss, read DB and set Redis with TTL 24h. With a Zipf-like distribution (a few viral links get most clicks), an 80/20 cache hit rate of 90%+ is typical, taking DB load from 12,000/s to under 1,200/s.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 455.2 130\" width=\"455.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cache aside on the redirect path\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M297.2 65 L353.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M297.2 65 L353.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M297.2 65 L353.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M297.2 65 L353.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Request</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redirect service</text><rect x=\"353.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"398.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis</text><rect x=\"353.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"398.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Link DB</text></svg><figcaption>Cache aside on the redirect path</figcaption></figure>\n<ul>\n<li>Redis config: <code>maxmemory 32gb</code>, <code>maxmemory-policy allkeys-lru</code>, 2 replicas.</li>\n<li><strong>Negative caching:</strong> cache 404s for 60 s to survive scans of random codes.</li>\n<li><strong>Hot key:</strong> a viral link could hit one Redis shard hard; add a tiny in-process cache (1 s TTL) on redirect servers.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Production incident pattern.</strong> Symptom: p99 latency jumps and DB CPU spikes after a celebrity tweet. Metric: cache hit ratio drops or one Redis shard's CPU is pinned. Fix: local cache + request coalescing (single flight) so 1,000 simultaneous misses cause one DB read.</p>\n<h3>Analytics without slowing redirects</h3>\n<p>On every redirect, publish <code>{code, ts, ip, userAgent, referrer}</code> to Kafka asynchronously (fire and forget, batched, <code>acks=1</code>). Workers aggregate per code per minute and write to ClickHouse/Druid or a counters table. If Kafka is down, drop events rather than fail the redirect: clicks are best effort, redirects are the product.</p>\n<h3>Expiry and cleanup</h3>\n<p>Store <code>expiresAt</code>. On read, check it and return 410. A nightly job deletes expired rows (or use DynamoDB TTL / Cassandra TTL). Do not recycle codes immediately; keep a tombstone window so an old shared link does not suddenly point to a stranger's page.</p>\n<h3>Abuse and security</h3>\n<p>Scan long URLs against Safe Browsing lists on creation and again periodically. Rate limit creates per API key and per IP. Do not allow <code>javascript:</code> or internal IP targets (SSRF/open-redirect abuse).</p>\n<h3>Pastebin variant</h3>\n<p>Same system, but the value is a text blob (up to 10 MB) instead of a URL. Differences:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Store content in <strong>object storage (S3)</strong> keyed by id, metadata (id, owner, expiry, visibility) in the DB.</li>\n<li>Size: 1M pastes/day x 10 KB average = 10 GB/day, 3.6 TB/year; dominated by blobs, so put S3 plus a CDN in front.</li>\n<li>Add a content hash to dedupe identical pastes.</li>\n<li>Support expiry options (10 min, 1 day, never) and private links (unguessable ID, longer, random).</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 440.8 130\" width=\"440.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pastebin: metadata in DB, content in object storage\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 65 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 96 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 96 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Paste API</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">CDN</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"366.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Metadata DB</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"74\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"366.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Object storage</text></svg><figcaption>Pastebin: metadata in DB, content in object storage</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry example.</strong> GitHub Gists and Pastebin.com keep text in object/file storage with metadata in a database.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> The key service is a drawer of pre-printed unique tickets that each cashier takes a stack of, so nobody ever hands out the same number twice.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hashing and ignoring collision handling.</li>\n<li>Sequential counter codes that expose how many links you have and are scrapeable.</li>\n<li>Letting analytics failures break redirects.</li>\n<li>Storing paste bodies in the database instead of blob storage.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"what-interviewers-look-for","title":"What interviewers look for","html":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Clarifying questions</strong> first: custom alias, expiry, analytics, scale.</li>\n<li><strong>Numbers</strong>: QPS, storage, and why 7 base62 characters.</li>\n<li><strong>A clear ID strategy</strong> with its trade-offs (hash vs counter vs key service) and collision handling.</li>\n<li><strong>Read-optimised design</strong>: cache aside, hit ratio reasoning, hot keys.</li>\n<li><strong>301 vs 302</strong> and what it implies for analytics.</li>\n<li><strong>Failure thinking</strong>: what if the ID service, Redis or Kafka is down; what degrades and what does not.</li>\n<li><strong>Seniors</strong> also mention abuse, GDPR deletion, multi-region reads, and the cost of each choice, and know which choices are reversible.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Jumping into sharding when the dataset is 2 TB.</li>\n<li>Not discussing security and abuse.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Tiny links are a key-value lookup: <code>code -> longUrl</code>; reads dominate 100:1, about 12k/s peak.</li>\n<li>7 base62 characters give 3.5 trillion codes; plenty for 6B links in 5 years.</li>\n<li>Pick the ID strategy deliberately: range allocator plus reversible scramble avoids collisions and guessability; it is the one-way door.</li>\n<li>Serve redirects from Redis (cache aside, negative caching, local cache for hot keys), DB as the source of truth.</li>\n<li>Use 302 if you need click analytics; send click events asynchronously through Kafka and never let them block the redirect.</li>\n<li>Pastebin = same design, but blob in S3, metadata in the DB, CDN in front.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}